- macOS desktop builds now ship as explicit architectures: an Apple Silicon (`arm64`) installer and a `universal` (arm64 + Intel) installer, each packaged with a matching Go sidecar (`lipo`-merged for the universal build). Previously the architecture was left to the build host, so Apple Silicon users could end up with an Intel app.
- The desktop app now finds user-installed `kubeconfig` exec plugins (for example `doctl`, `aws`, or `gcloud` from Homebrew) when it is launched from Finder/LaunchServices. The Go server is spawned with the usual Homebrew and `/usr/local` bin directories prepended to `PATH`, instead of the minimal launchd `PATH` that GUI apps inherit.
- Empty page-level sections (for example Gateway API in a namespace without Gateways, HTTP Routes, or GRPC Routes) now show a "no resources were found" placeholder instead of a blank page. The placeholder is only added when the section is the page itself, so combined pages such as the namespace overview do not show a message for every empty subsection.
